PARTS=[
 {"t":"The Top: Who Sits Above the Congregation","d":"A few headquarters appoint the leaders, hold the money and control the holy places for a large share of the world's believers."},
 {"t":"The State: What Governments Use Religion For","d":"One layer down, the government holds a power no church has: it can make a faith official, pay for it from taxes and punish people who leave it."},
 {"t":"The Sellers: How the Blessing Is Sold","d":"Between the headquarters and the believer stand the people who ask for the money: the preacher on television and the agency that sells the pilgrimage."},
 {"t":"The Owners: Land, Tax and the Books Nobody Sees","d":"Religious bodies are landlords and investors. In many countries the law lets them keep their accounts closed and their property untaxed."},
 {"t":"The Flock: What Happens to the Member","d":"When a member is harmed, the record shows what the institution protected first: its name, its money and its clergy."},
 {"t":"The Ballot: Faith as a Political Machine","d":"A congregation is also a list of voters. Parties court it, and religious money crosses borders to change other countries' laws."},
 {"t":"The Pushback: Where It Was Reversed","d":"Voters, courts, regulators and millions of members who walked out have undone parts of the chain."},
]

FLOWS=[]
def flow(**k): FLOWS.append(k)
